---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Header from '../components/Header.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
---

<Layout title="About" description="Learn about CheckYourCalendar, its mission to bridge utility and cultural storytelling, and the science behind calendar conversions.">
  <Header activeTab="about" />

  <main class="container main-content">
    <article class="editorial-article">
      <header class="article-header">
        <h1 class="article-title">About CheckYourCalendar</h1>
        <p class="article-subtitle">Bridging mathematical coordinates and cultural stories</p>
      </header>

      <section class="article-body">
        <p class="lead">
          Time is not merely a number. Every day has a context. Every date has a history. Yet, timekeeping sites are traditionally split between dry utility grids and hyper-siloed religious portals. CheckYourCalendar exists to bridge that gap.
        </p>

        <h2>Our Mission: The Date Discovery Path</h2>
        <p>
          We operate under a simple, progressive information architecture:
        </p>
        <div class="mission-path">
          <div class="path-step">
            <span class="step-num">1</span>
            <strong>Date</strong>
            <p>A specific coordinate in time</p>
          </div>
          <div class="path-arrow"><span class="material-symbols-outlined">arrow_forward</span></div>
          <div class="path-step">
            <span class="step-num">2</span>
            <strong>Calendar</strong>
            <p>How different cultures map that date</p>
          </div>
          <div class="path-arrow"><span class="material-symbols-outlined">arrow_forward</span></div>
          <div class="path-step">
            <span class="step-num">3</span>
            <strong>Observance</strong>
            <p>What festivals or fasts occur today</p>
          </div>
          <div class="path-arrow"><span class="material-symbols-outlined">arrow_forward</span></div>
          <div class="path-step">
            <span class="step-num">4</span>
            <strong>Meaning & Context</strong>
            <p>The cultural and historical significance behind it</p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <p>
          CheckYourCalendar is designed to let you check a conversion instantly, but walk away with a deeper understanding of what today actually represents across human traditions.
        </p>

        <h2 id="methodology">Calculation Methodology</h2>
        <p>
          Calendar calculations are complex and high-trust. We utilize standard, open-source astronomical and mathematical adapters to compute dates programmatically:
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Solar Calendars</strong> (e.g., Gregorian, Persian) use precise solar cycle calculations, mapping astronomical coordinates or leap rules directly.</li>
          <li><strong>Lunisolar Calendars</strong> (e.g., Hebrew, Chinese) balance the lunar cycles with solar correction. We use official astronomical models to calculate leap additions and seasonal adjustments.</li>
          <li><strong>Pure Lunar Calendars</strong> (e.g., Hijri) follow the moon sighting cycle. For calculation predictability, we utilize the Umm al-Qura calendar civil calculations as a standard, while clearly documenting that visual sighting variances may differ by 1 day regionally.</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>Research & Verification Standards</h2>
        <p>
          We hold cultural and religious content to high accuracy standards:
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>No Mass AI Filler:</strong> All descriptions and stories are curated and fact-checked. We do not mass-generate spiritual claims or historical legends.</li>
          <li><strong>Attribution:</strong> We reference academic publications, government registries, and established cultural/religious archives.</li>
          <li><strong>Neutral Tone:</strong> We present cultural and religious traditions informatively and respectfully, without promotion or sectarian bias.</li>
        </ul>
      </section>
    </article>
  </main>

  <Footer />
</Layout>

<style>
  .main-content {
    padding-top: var(--spacing-xl);
    padding-bottom: var(--spacing-xl);
  }

  .editorial-article {
    max-width: 720px;
    margin: 0 auto;
  }

  .article-header {
    border-bottom: 2px solid var(--color-primary);
    padding-bottom: var(--spacing-md);
    margin-bottom: var(--spacing-lg);
  }

  .article-title {
    font-family: var(--font-serif);
    font-size: 2.5rem;
    color: var(--color-primary);
    line-height: 1.15;
  }

  .article-subtitle {
    font-family: var(--font-sans);
    font-size: 1.125rem;
    font-style: italic;
    color: var(--color-on-surface-variant);
    margin-top: var(--spacing-xs);
  }

  .article-body {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: var(--spacing-md);
  }

  .lead {
    font-size: 1.125rem;
    line-height: 1.6;
    color: var(--color-on-background);
    font-weight: 500;
  }

  .article-body h2 {
    font-family: var(--font-serif);
    font-size: 1.625rem;
    color: var(--color-primary);
    margin-top: var(--spacing-md);
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-outline-variant);
    padding-bottom: var(--spacing-xs);
  }

  .article-body p {
    font-size: 0.9375rem;
    line-height: 1.6;
    color: var(--color-on-background);
  }

  .article-body ul {
    list-style-type: square;
    padding-left: var(--spacing-lg);
    font-size: 0.9375rem;
    color: var(--color-on-background);
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: var(--spacing-xs);
  }

  /* Mission Path Bento style timeline */
  .mission-path {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: var(--spacing-sm);
    background-color: var(--color-surface-dim);
    padding: var(--spacing-md);
    border-radius: var(--radius-md);
    margin: var(--spacing-sm) 0;
  }

  .path-step {
    background-color: var(--color-surface);
    border: 1px solid var(--color-outline);
    border-radius: var(--radius-sm);
    padding: var(--spacing-md);
    position: relative;
  }

  .step-num {
    position: absolute;
    top: var(--spacing-xs);
    right: var(--spacing-sm);
    font-family: var(--font-serif);
    font-size: 1.5rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    color: var(--color-primary-container);
    opacity: 0.5;
  }

  .path-step strong {
    font-family: var(--font-serif);
    color: var(--color-primary);
    font-size: 1.125rem;
  }

  .path-step p {
    font-size: 0.8125rem;
    color: var(--color-on-surface-variant);
    margin-top: 4px;
  }

  .path-arrow {
    display: none;
    justify-content: center;
    color: var(--color-outline-variant);
  }

  @media (min-width: 768px) {
    .mission-path {
      flex-direction: row;
      align-items: center;
      justify-content: space-between;
    }

    .path-step {
      width: 22%;
      min-height: 120px;
    }

    .path-arrow {
      display: flex;
    }
  }
</style>
